WEBVTT

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.760
RALPH: Okay. My turn, my turn.
Um, I got one.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.160
VANELLOPE:
Great, but can you make it

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:54.440
a little more challenging
this time?

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:57.720
RALPH: Okay. Check this out.
(CLEARS THROAT)

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:01.600
I spy with my little eye...

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.080
something yellow...

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:09.360
and round, and it eats dots.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.680
VANELLOPE: (SCOFFS)
Seriously, Ralph?

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.200
RALPH: Yeah, seriously.
You're never gonna get it.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.880
VANELLOPE: Well, obviously,
it's Pac-Man.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.240
RALPH: No, that's not...

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:19.680
Why is that obvious?

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:21.600
Name one other thing
in this whole arcade

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.080
that is yellow and round
and eats dots.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:25.320
I can name two things.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:26.800
Ms. Pac-Man and Baby Pac-Man.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:28.560
Boom! I accept your apology.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:31.760
Yeah, you're right. Okay.
But was it Pac-Man?

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.920
-Yeah, you got me.
-(VANELLOPE LAUGHS)

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.680
VANELLOPE: Knew it.
All right, riddle me this...

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:40.400
do you or do you not think
that Zangief waxes?

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.520
No way. Look at the guy.
He looks like a yeti.

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:43.680
I don't know.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:46.000
I mean, if the fur
were confined to his chest,

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.120
I might agree...

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.720
but look at those
two very specific

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.080
tuffets of shin hair...

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:51.400
poking out of his boots.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:54.440
That does not just happen,
Ralph. That is a choice.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:56.360
RALPH:
You're totally right, kid.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:58.920
He's baby smooth
everywhere else.

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:00.920
I rest my case.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:03.360
My mind is blown!

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:04.960
Let's go get a root beer.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.000
RALPH: (SIGHS) Okay, let's see
what you got, kid.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:09.720
-(BURPS)
-Ooh!

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:11.920
Nice one. Okay.
(CLEARS THROAT)

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.640
I think I got one
in the chamber.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:16.480
-(BURPS LOUDLY)
-Ew!

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:18.360
-Gross.
-Thank you.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:19.800
Hey, wanna sneak into Tron?

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:21.640
Doesn't that game
have a virus?

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:23.480
No. I'm sure they fixed it.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:25.840
-(LASERS ZAPPING)
-VANELLOPE: Whoo!

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.440
I'm gonna beat
my speed record!

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:30.120
Hey, wait for me!

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.040
(VANELLOPE WHOOPING)

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:38.080
(DISTORTED WHOOPING)

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.320
VANELLOPE: Ralph.

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:41.520
RALPH: Yeah?

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:44.000
VANELLOPE: I don't think
they fixed the game.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:46.240
RALPH: Uh... No.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:48.240
Help!

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:50.560
Hey, Tron!

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:52.120
Tronny!

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:54.880
Tronny boy!

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:56.880
Help!

00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:58.920
VANELLOPE: Do you realize

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.560
we're basically
just, like, zeroes and ones...

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:05.120
floating around the universe
like tiny specks of dust?

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:06.960
Like, doesn't the very nature

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.440
of our existence
make you wonder...

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.760
if there's more to life
than this?

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:12.960
Why would I wonder
if there's more to life

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:14.880
when the life
I got is perfect?

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:17.520
I mean, sure.
Doesn't look so hot on paper.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:19.760
I'm just a bad guy
from some old video game

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:20.880
who wrecks a building.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:22.360
And yeah, for 27 years,

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.480
I was a total zero
without any friends.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:26.880
But now,
I got a best friend...

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.200
who just happens to be

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:30.000
the coolest kid
in the whole arcade.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:32.000
Aw, thanks, pal.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:33.160
Watch this.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:35.200
(GRUNTS)

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.160
-(BUZZING)
-RALPH: Home run!

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:38.880
All right,
let's go watch the sunrise.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:40.960
VANELLOPE:
Are you really saying

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.200
there's not one single,
solitary thing...

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:45.280
about your life
that you would change?

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:47.360
RALPH: Well, think about it.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:50.000
You and me get to
goof off all night long.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:52.800
Litwak shows up, we go to
work, we put in our hours.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:54.280
Then the arcade closes

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:56.000
and we get to do it
all over again.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.680
The only thing I might do
different in that scenario...

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.720
would be not having
to go to work.

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:03.840
Other than that, (CHUCKLES)
I wouldn't change a thing.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:05.040
Huh?

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.800
Hey, where'd our sunrise go?

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:10.600
MR. LITWAK: All right,
let's get you plugged in.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.160
(BEEPING)

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:14.120
(GASPS)
That's a plug-in alert.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:16.400
Litwak hasn't plugged in
a new game in forever.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:18.600
-Let's go see what it is!
-Yeah!

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:20.680
RALPH: Excuse us. Excuse us.
Minor emergency.

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:23.120
Hey, Felix, Calhoun,
what's getting plugged in?

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:24.640
Well, Ralph, Sonic thinks

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:26.640
it's gonna be
a new pinball machine.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:28.160
What do you think, lady love?

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:32.000
I'll bet you a shiny nickel
it's a blood pressure machine.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.160
-Kids love those things.
-RALPH: Ooh.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:35.280
(ALARM BLARING)

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:37.800
Please be a racing game.
Please be a racing game.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.840
Please be a racing game.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:44.520
"Whiffee"? Or, "Wifey"?

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.600
Well, it's either wiffle ball,
or an arranged marriage game.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.760
It's actually pronounced
"Wi-Fi," Ralph.

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:50.920
Yeah, that's what I said.

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:52.440
And Wi-Fi is the Internet...

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:53.800
which is an online community

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:55.080
where human beings
go to shop...

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:57.000
and play games and socialize.

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:58.520
Ooh, fun!

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:00.080
Oh, no, it is not.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.360
That sign right there
says "Wi-Fi."

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:04.880
What it should say
is "Die-Fi."

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:06.000
(CHUCKLES)

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:08.840
That's a little humor there.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.160
But seriously, the Internet
is nothing to laugh at.

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:12.960
It is new, it is different,

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:14.360
and therefore
we should fear it.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:16.720
So keep out, for Pete's sake,
and get to work.

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:18.640
The arcade's about to open.

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:21.520
Figures, we finally get
something new plugged in...

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:23.640
and we're not even allowed
to go in there.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:25.400
Totally not fair.

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:28.200
A new racing game
would've been cool.

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:29.400
Something wrong
with your game?

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:30.560
No, no.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:33.280
It's just every bonus level's
been unlocked.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:35.200
I know every shortcut.

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:37.640
Man, I'd kill for even
just a new track.

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:40.680
New track? You already got,
like, three choices.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.320
Yeah, I know,
but don't you ever wish

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:43.440
something new and different...

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:45.040
would happen in your game?

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:46.120
Nope.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:49.120
Really?
Well, agree to disagree.

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:50.800
Wait, I don't wanna disagree.

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:52.600
No, no.
It's just a fancy way to say

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:54.240
we don't have to
argue about it.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:56.080
We're arguing?
I don't wanna argue.

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:58.560
Relax. Stop making it a thing.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:01.400
Go to work. I'll see you
tonight, stench vessel.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:02.560
All right.

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:04.000
(SIGHS)

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:10.200
She wants a new track,
I'll give her a new track.

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:12.400
(WHIRRING)

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.600
SWATI: Come on, Nafisa!
Let's play Sugar Rush!

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:20.600
Pick Vanellope, Swati.
She's got the best superpower.

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:23.240
Yeah, the glitch. I love her.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:24.320
ANNOUNCER: Drivers,

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.240
-start your engines.
-(ENGINES REVVING)

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:29.080
You're gonna lose today,
Princess.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:32.240
While, yes, I am technically
a princess, Taffyta...

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:35.440
I'd rather you just think of
me as plain old Vanellope...

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:37.720
the racer who's about to
kick your butt.

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:41.000
ANNOUNCER:
Three, two, one, go!

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:43.400
(TIRES SCREECHING)

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:48.040
And pardon me, excuse me,
coming through.

